title: FabianParadeDialogue
tags:
---

<< if DoesHeKnow ("SpokenToFabianParade") >>
	<<jump ReturningFabianParade >>
<<endif>>

SETTING - Beside a bridge that juts out into the great expense of the void lake. The Parade ends here.

AT RISE - FABIAN looking here and there, as if trying to find somewhere he can help, but ending up stuck in paralysis. Once approached, he stops turning.


<< if $FabianMood lte -2 >> //Unhappy
	FABIAN: (Visibly hesitant) I’m glad to see that you came, Sasha. Have you talked to your brother yet?
<< elif $FabianMood gte 2>> //Happy
	FABIAN: (smiling, attempting to wave with one hand) Sasha! Just who I wanted to see!
<< else >> //Perfectly neutral
	FABIAN: (nods) Sasha! I’d give a wave, but my hands are currently occupied.
<< endif >>

-> ”What are you holding?”
    SASHA: ”What are you holding?”
	FABIAN: (stammers slightly) It’s the urn.
	FABIAN: Alfonz’s urn.
-> ”Is that his…?”
    SASHA: ”Is that his…?”
	FABIAN: Yes. It’s Alfonz.

<< if $FabianMood lte -2 >> //Unhappy
	FABIAN: (averts gaze) I'm sorry for your loss.
<< elif $FabianMood gte 2>> //Happy
	FABIAN: (cheerful smile slowly fades) I'm sorry for your loss.
<< else >> //Perfectly neutral
	FABIAN: (polite smile fades) I'm sorry for your loss.
<< endif >>



<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
	PSY: Avoiding eye contact, a sign of shame, a feeling that you have done something wrong.
	PSY: Does he feel that he is intruding in your reunion with Alfonz? 
    PSY: Or perhaps is he ashamed that this is the best reunion he can provide for you with your old friend?
    PSY: His shoulders shrink, he makes himself small. A feeling of inadequacy, powerlessness. It’s the latter.
    PSY: It's only now that you realise that you misjudged.
    PSY: You are projecting. It is you who is feeling small. So, so small.
    PSY: You stomach twists. Your breathing is tense, and fast, and faster, and faster.
    PSY: Act normal. You know how to act normal. You studied this. This is what you know. Focus.
    PSY: You wipe your eyes, and steady your nerves. You'll be okay. 
<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
	ART: It is an odd sort of reunion. Instead of Alfonz, you are greeting this painted mimicry of him. 
    ART: In the details you can see subtle changes to him in the years you were away. 
    ART: His hands gained more wrinkles. His garb gained more creases. The most crucial part is left to your imagination.
    ART: You try filling in that detail. From the recesses of your memory, you project Alfonz's face onto the blank canvas.
    ART: His friendly, smiling face, looking into your eyes.
    ART: His smiling face that you have not seen in years.
    ART: His face that you will never see again.
    ART: His face that you have been denied a final chance to glimpse.
    ART: His crying, twisting face... No, no, he didn't cry. He's not the one crying.
    ART: Fabian says nothing, and gives you some needed space.
    ART: Your sleeve is a little wetter now. But you are okay. It's just a wooden urn.
<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
	TECH: The urn is handcrafted. You can see flaws in the woodwork that a factory build would lack. Some stone seems to be worked into it too, to allow it to sink.
	TECH: The painting of the urns is done by those close to the defunct, so it makes sense that their construction would be too.
	TECH: why does the urn look so shabby? Why are the edges so sharp, why is the varnish so sloppy?
    TECH: Did they not care? Did they not care at all about the vessel where your dead, gone friend would be laid to rest?
    TECH: He doesn't deserve this. He deserves so, so much more. He deserves the best, most perfect urn that he could have gotten.
    TECH: He didn't deserve any of this. He didn't deserve to die. He didn't need to die. Not before you could ever meet him again.
    TECH: Not before you could have met him again, seen him again, saw how he looked now so you could make him the best urn in the whole damn world.
    TECH: You feel your heart beating fast. Indignation flows through your veins. 
    TECH: You need to channel this feeling into something, do something with it, you have to. You feel like exploding, like blowing up, like destroying something.
    TECH: You need... You need to calm down. You focus your breathing, slower, and slower. This is no time for anger.
    TECH: You wipe your eyes and steady yourself. You are in control again. You'll be okay.
<< endif >>

<< jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>





===

title: FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1
---

<<if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes == true && $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face == true>>
	<<jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Cont>>
<<else>>
	-> “Is there anything inside? Since there can’t be any ashes...” << if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes == false >>
		SASHA: “Is there anything inside? Since there can’t be any ashes...”
		FABIAN: There is. When we have no ashes to put in an urn, we put a star token inside to represent them.
		FABIAN: One of the members of his congregation made it with clay. A girl who cared quite strongly about him. Said he was like a father to her.
		FABIAN: I wish you could have seen it before we sealed the urn. It was quite beautiful.
		<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
			You feel the weight of four years of history that you missed in his words. 
			You are far from the last person Alfonz made an impact on
		<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
			You feel the weight of four years of history that you missed in his words.
			Almost pettily, your brain insists that you would have made it even more beautiful than she did.
		<< elseif $TechMajor == true>>
			You feel the weight of four years of history that you missed in his words.
			Though if people cared so much, why was the urn so damn imperfect?
		<<endif>>
		<< set $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes = true >>
		<< jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>
	-> “Why does it have no face?” << if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face == false >>
		SASHA: “Why does it have no face?”
		FABIAN: Oh, right. The face…
		FABIAN: (slowly, hesitantly) It was your brother’s idea. He thought you’d like to be the one to paint his face onto the urn.
		FABIAN: We did think that you’d arrive a little sooner.
		FABIAN: But it was just an unfortunate miscommunication. (quickly adds) There is nobody to blame here.
		<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
			Alfonz is going to be sent off faceless, muted, and blind, and it is your fault.
		<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
			Alfonz is going to be sent off faceless, muted, and blind, and it is your fault.
		<< elseif $TechMajor == true>>
			Alfonz is going to be sent off faceless, muted, and blind, and it is your fault.
		<<endif>>
		<<set $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face = true>>
		<< jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>
<<endif>>

===

title: FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Cont
---

	FABIAN: Right, your brother… Did you find him? I haven’t seen him around yet, though I only just got here.
	
	<< if DoesHeKnow ("DmitriyTarot") >>
		<<jump SeenDmitriyParadeTime>>
	<<else>>
		<< Learn SpokenToFabianParade >>
		-> "No.."
			SASHA: "No.."
			Fabian: (slight surprise) Ah, well that's all right. I'm sure he's around here somewhere- speak to him first, and then we can talk about the parade.
		-> "Yes, I did."
			SASHA: "Yes, I did."
			FABIAN: Oh, really?"
			FABIAN: (slightly unsure) Well.. uh..
			FABIAN: How about you come ask him to join us and watch the parade? I'm sure his break is over by now.
			NARRATOR: Tough luck, Fabian has a sixth sense for liars.
	<<endif>>


===
title: ReturningFabianParade
---
FABIAN: Ah, hello Sasha. Have you spoken to your brother yet?

	<< if DoesHeKnow ("DmitriyTarot") >>
		<<jump SeenDmitriyParadeTime>>
	<<else>>
		-> "Not yet."
		-> "Oh, right. That's what I was doing."
	<<endif>>
	
	
	
===
title: SeenDmitriyParadeTime
---
    -> “I did, just a moment ago.”
        SASHA: “I did, just a moment ago.”
        FABIAN: Oh really? Wonderful! I was worried you wouldn’t be able to see him at all, that’s a relief.
        FABIAN: So, how was it talking to him again?
        -> “He was distant.”
            SASHA: “He was distant.”
        	FABIAN: Really? I… Well… (trails off into silence)
	        FABIAN: I’m really sorry Sasha.
	        FABIAN: He’ll come around. I’m sure he just needs a bit of time.
	        << if $FabianMood gte 1 >>
	        	<< set $FabianMood -= 1 >>
	        << elseif $FabianMood lte -1 >>
	        	<< set $FabianMood += 1 >>
	        << endif >>
        -> “Same as I remembered him.”
            SASHA: “Same as I remembered him.”
	        FABIAN: So he’s always been the same jolly chum I see! 
	        FABIAN: He’s a bit of a closed book sometimes, but I knew he’d cheer up when seeing his lost sibling again.
            << set $FabianMood += 1 >>
        -> “None of your business.”
            SASHA: “None of your business.”
		    FABIAN: (startled) Alright, no need to be so harsh about it.
		    FABIAN: If you’d rather keep this to yourself, I understand.
            << set $FabianMood -= 1 >>
    ->  “I don’t want to talk about it.”
        SASHA: “I don’t want to talk about it.”
        FABIAN: Oh, alright. I hope that isn’t a bad sign
        FABIAN: If you haven’t found him yet, we can go look for him together later, after the parade.
    << set $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face = true >>

	-> “When does the Parade start?”
		SASHA: “When does the Parade start?”
		FABIAN: (while looking around) I think it will still be a few hours. Most of the other participants of the parade still have to arrive too.
		FABIAN: Babushka still needs to come from the River district, and she’ll need help to carry her urn here.
		FABIAN: If you wish, you can find a good seat already and wait for the parade to begin.
		-> “Sure. I’ll just wait until the parade”
			SASHA: “Sure. I’ll just wait until the parade”
			FABIAN: Wonderful! I really hope you enjoy it. 
			FABIAN: Now if you excuse me, I need to go find someone to help Babushka as I said...
        << Loop >>
		

===
